From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] extmod/vfs_lfsx: statvfs on littlefs v2 counts each
 directory once.

os.statvfs() on a littlefs v2 filesystem reported two blocks too few free
for every directory, so a board with many folders in /lib and /apps could
show a negative free count while it still had room. statvfs counted the
blocks lfs2_fs_traverse() visits, and that visits each directory's
metadata pair twice: once along the chain of pairs, and once from its
parent's entry. lfs2_fs_size() makes the same walk without the second
visit, and it's what littlefs offers for this count. The allocator's own
walk is unchanged: marking a block twice there does no harm.

An ESP32-P4 board's 7.27 MB filesystem, read out whole, has 654 files and
99 directories. Mounted by the unix port's VfsLfs2 before this change,
statvfs gave -89 free blocks of 1776; with it, 109, the count
littlefs-python gives for the same image. The tests/extmod vfs tests pass
on the unix port, with vfs_lfs.py's expected output moving from 7 free
blocks to 9 once its one directory is counted once.

Based-on: micropython b70ae1aca (v1.30.0-preview-160)
---
 extmod/vfs_lfsx.c           | 11 +++++++++--
 tests/extmod/vfs_lfs.py.exp |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/extmod/vfs_lfsx.c b/extmod/vfs_lfsx.c
--- a/extmod/vfs_lfsx.c
+++ b/extmod/vfs_lfsx.c
@@ -414,21 +414,28 @@ static mp_obj_t MP_VFS_LFSx(stat)(mp_obj_t self_in, mp_obj_t path_in) {
 }
 static MP_DEFINE_CONST_FUN_OBJ_2(MP_VFS_LFSx(stat_obj), MP_VFS_LFSx(stat));
 
+#if LFS_BUILD_VERSION == 1
 static int LFSx_API(traverse_cb)(void *data, LFSx_API(block_t) bl) {
     (void)bl;
     uint32_t *n = (uint32_t *)data;
     *n += 1;
     return LFSx_MACRO(_ERR_OK);
 }
+#endif
 
 static mp_obj_t MP_VFS_LFSx(statvfs)(mp_obj_t self_in, mp_obj_t path_in) {
     (void)path_in;
     MP_OBJ_VFS_LFSx *self = MP_OBJ_TO_PTR(self_in);
-    uint32_t n_used_blocks = 0;
     #if LFS_BUILD_VERSION == 1
+    uint32_t n_used_blocks = 0;
     int ret = LFSx_API(traverse)(&self->lfs, LFSx_API(traverse_cb), &n_used_blocks);
     #else
-    int ret = LFSx_API(fs_traverse)(&self->lfs, LFSx_API(traverse_cb), &n_used_blocks);
+    // lfs2_fs_traverse() visits each directory's metadata pair twice, once
+    // along the chain of pairs and once from its parent's entry, so
+    // counting its blocks reports 2 blocks too many for every directory.
+    // lfs2_fs_size() counts each block once.
+    LFSx_API(ssize_t) ret = LFSx_API(fs_size)(&self->lfs);
+    uint32_t n_used_blocks = ret;
     #endif
     if (ret < 0) {
         mp_raise_OSError(-ret);
diff --git a/tests/extmod/vfs_lfs.py.exp b/tests/extmod/vfs_lfs.py.exp
--- a/tests/extmod/vfs_lfs.py.exp
+++ b/tests/extmod/vfs_lfs.py.exp
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@ write 0
 write 1
 write 2
 write 3
-(1024, 1024, 30, 7, 7, 0, 0, 0, 0, 255)
+(1024, 1024, 30, 9, 9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 255)
 [('test', 32768, 0, 8), ('testbig2', 32768, 0, 16384), ('testdir', 16384, 0, 0)]
 [('testbig2', 32768, 0, 16384)]
 [('test', 32768, 0, 8), ('testbig2', 32768, 0, 16384), ('testdir', 16384, 0, 0)]
